{{Quote box
| quote = It is often assumed that in a conflict there are two sides in opposition to one another, and that a person who is not actively committed to one side must be supporting the other. During the course of a conflict, leaders on both sides will use this argument to gain active support from the "crowd". In reality, conflicts involving more than two persons usually have more than two sides, and if a resistance movement is to be successful, propaganda and politicization are essential.<ref name="Pirouet 1977 197">{{Harvnb|Pirouet|1977|p=[https://books.google.com/books?id=uZY3AAAAIAAJ&pg=PA197 197]}}.</ref>
